From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.ui.xaml: panels -- Panel, Grid, StackPanel, Border

XAML pages are built of panels; there were none. Panel (composable: applications derive their own) with Children, a UIElementCollection that makes its items the panel's visual children (one parent each); Grid with RowDefinitions/ColumnDefinitions in pixels, Auto (to the content) and stars (shares of the rest, within Min/Max), Row/Column/RowSpan/ColumnSpan, Padding, RowSpacing/ColumnSpacing; StackPanel (Orientation, Spacing, Padding); Border (BorderThickness and Padding around its Child; brushes kept for drawing). One collection implementation (IVector/IVectorView/IIterable/IIterator, live views) serves them, with the parameterized interfaces' IIDs from their type signatures. Interface identity per windows-rs 0.30.0 (MIT OR Apache-2.0); layout behaviour per the classes' public documentation; the implementation is ours. Behind the XAML switch of 6131.
---
